Validate and install a workflow YAML file.

The file is parsed and compiled, then copied into the CLI's
config directory as <id>.yaml, named after its own `id:`
field. That installed copy — not <path> — is what
`workflow run`/`workflow list` use afterward, so editing
<path> later has no effect until you run `add` again.
Every file must declare a `workflow_protocol_version` field
naming the workflow YAML protocol version it targets;
`ags workflow template` fills this in automatically.
Use --validate-only to check the file without installing it.

Usage:
  workflow add [OPTIONS] <path>

Arguments:
  <path>
          Path to the workflow YAML file

Options:
      --validate-only
          Validate without installing

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
